     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the maximum, so I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day. Single doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest common tablet strength.\n- **Risk:** at twice the maximum daily dose, there is a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO two or three times daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. I'd still recommend a pharmacy review."
      }
     ],
